# M9.1 acceptance: keyboard shortcuts for the agent chat. Run through
# tests/acceptance/m9.1.sh (fixture, scratch HOME, slow fake sidecar).
#
# Layout these coordinates assume (1400x900 window at the screen origin, no
# window manager, as in m5.2.steps and m6.4.steps): project panel x 0..225,
# PDF pane x 225..980, chat pane x 980..1400. The chat input is at about
# (1180, 800), Send and Stop in the row below it, the message view covers
# (1190, 300). The PDF view is at (600, 600).
#
# Interface choices where the spec is silent:
#   - The menu bar title is "&Chat", so Alt+C opens the Chat menu. Its items
#     are "&New Chat\tCtrl+N", "&Focus Chat Input\tCtrl+L", a separator, and
#     "&Stop Reply" (no accelerator in the label; Esc is wired in the frame).
#   - A reply is slow: one text_delta every 0.5 s, 40 pieces (about 20 s).
#   - "permit" in a prompt makes the fake ask for a Write permission on
#     notes.md, so the permission dialog opens and waits for an answer.
#   - Clicking outside an open menu closes it. The steps do not press Esc
#     with a menu open, because the menu takes Esc for itself.
wait 4

# Start: the PDF shows paper.pdf page 1, the project panel lists paper.pdf,
# the chat pane is empty with an empty input and Send enabled. No red notice.
shot start

key alt+c
wait 1

# The Chat menu is open below the menu bar, between Project and Help. It lists
# "New Chat" with Ctrl+N, "Focus Chat Input" with Ctrl+L, a separator, then
# "Stop Reply", greyed out because no reply runs. All items show their labels.
shot chat-menu-idle

click 1190 300
wait 1

click 600 600
key ctrl+l
type PDF-FOCUS
wait 1

# Ctrl+L pressed with the PDF view focused moved the caret into the chat input:
# the text "PDF-FOCUS" appears in the input at the bottom of the chat pane. The
# PDF page shows no typed text. No reply was sent, no red notice.
shot focus-from-pdf

key ctrl+a
key BackSpace
click 110 300
key ctrl+l
type PANEL-FOCUS
wait 1

# Same from the project panel (clicked at (110, 300)): "PANEL-FOCUS" is in the
# chat input, and the project panel shows no typed text.
shot focus-from-panel

key ctrl+a
key BackSpace
click 1190 300
key ctrl+l
type VIEW-FOCUS
wait 1

# Same from the message view: "VIEW-FOCUS" is in the chat input. The message
# view shows no typed text and no message was sent.
shot focus-from-view

key ctrl+a
key BackSpace
click 1180 800
type IDLE-ESC
key Escape
wait 1

# Esc with no reply running does nothing. The input still reads "IDLE-ESC".
# The message view is empty: no grey "Stopped." line, no red notice.
shot escape-idle

key ctrl+a
key BackSpace
click 1180 800
type SLOW reply please
key Return
wait 3

# Mid-stream: the message view shows "SLOW reply please" and the reply's
# "Slow part N of 40." pieces, a few of them (about 4 to 8). Stop is enabled,
# Send is greyed out. The input is empty.
shot slow-streaming

key Escape
wait 2

# Esc stopped the reply. The pieces already shown stay, and a grey "Stopped."
# line follows them. The reply has fewer than 40 pieces. Send is enabled, Stop
# is greyed out. No red notice.
shot esc-stopped

click 1180 800
type SLOW menu check
key Return
wait 3
key ctrl+n
wait 1

# A second reply runs ("SLOW menu check" and its pieces are in the view). Ctrl+N
# pressed during the reply did nothing: the same messages are still shown, the
# reply keeps streaming, and no new empty chat appears.
shot ctrl-n-while-running

key alt+c
wait 1

# The Chat menu while the reply runs: "New Chat Ctrl+N" is greyed out,
# "Focus Chat Input Ctrl+L" is enabled, and "Stop Reply" is enabled.
shot chat-menu-running

click 1190 300
wait 1
click 1180 800
wait 1
key Escape
wait 2

# Esc from the input stopped this reply: a grey "Stopped." line follows
# "SLOW menu check" and its pieces. No red notice.
shot esc-stopped-2

key ctrl+n
wait 2

# Ctrl+N with no reply running started a new chat. The message view is empty
# (the earlier messages are not shown). The chat list has a new untitled entry
# selected. No red notice.
shot ctrl-n-new-chat

click 1180 800
type permit a write to notes
key Return
wait 2

# A permission dialog for the Write tool (notes.md) is open over the window.
# Esc belongs to this dialog here, so it must still be on screen.
shot permission-dialog

key Escape
wait 3

# Esc denied the request: the dialog is gone. The message view shows "Checking
# permission.", then "Permission reply: deny.", and the reply ended with Send
# enabled and Stop greyed out. No "Stopped." line and no red notice.
shot permission-denied
